RESOLUTION OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS OF YUHAN HOESA (LIMITED LIABILITY COMPANY) ADOPTED BY UNANIMOUS WRITTEN CONSENT IN LIEU OF A MEETING PURSUANT TO ARTICLE 287-36 OF THE KOREAN COMMERCIAL ACT

WHEREAS, the undersigned, being all the directors of Yuhan Hoesa (the 'Company'), a limited liability company organized under the laws of the Republic of Korea, have consented to the adoption of the following resolutions without a formal meeting, as permitted by law and the Company's Articles of Incorporation;

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED, that the Company hereby subscribes to and accepts the initial share capital of KRW 100,000,000 (One Hundred Million Korean Won) divided into 100,000 shares of par value KRW 1,000 each, which shares are fully paid in cash to the Company's designated bank account, and the issuance of such shares to the initial shareholders is hereby ratified and confirmed;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the registered office of the Company shall be established at [Insert Full Address in Seoul, South Korea], and the Company shall file all necessary registrations with the competent Court Registry and tax authorities;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the following persons are hereby appointed as the initial statutory officers of the Company: (a) [Name] as Chief Executive Officer and Representative Director, (b) [Name] as Chief Financial Officer, and (c) [Name] as Compliance Officer, each to serve until their successors are duly elected and qualified;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall open and maintain bank accounts with [Bank Name] and [Bank Name], and the CEO and CFO are jointly authorized to execute all banking documents, sign checks, and initiate wire transfers, subject to the Company's internal control policies and applicable law;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall apply for all necessary licenses and permits, including the Money Exchange Business License under the Foreign Exchange Transactions Act and the Electronic Financial Transaction License under the Electronic Financial Transactions Act, and the CEO is authorized to execute all applications and agreements related thereto;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall adopt a corporate seal (인장) and register it with the registry, and the CEO shall have custody of the seal;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall engage external legal counsel and certified public accountants to ensure compliance with all statutory and regulatory requirements, and the CFO is authorized to approve their fees;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall adopt a comprehensive anti-money laundering (AML) and know-your-customer (KYC) policy, and the Compliance Officer shall be responsible for its implementation and for filing all suspicious transaction reports with the Financial Intelligence Unit (FIU) of Korea;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall maintain all corporate records, including minutes, share register, and financial statements, at the registered office, and shall make them available for inspection as required by law;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall indemnify its directors and officers to the fullest extent permitted by law, and shall purchase directors and officers liability insurance;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall file all required tax registrations with the National Tax Service and obtain a business registration certificate (사업자등록증) within 20 days of incorporation;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall comply with all applicable data protection and privacy laws, including the Personal Information Protection Act, in connection with its remittance services;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall establish a compliance committee to review all cross-border transactions and ensure adherence to the Foreign Exchange Transactions Act and the Financial Transactions Reports Act;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall maintain a minimum capital reserve as required by the Financial Services Commission and shall not distribute dividends unless such reserve is maintained;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall appoint a registered agent for service of process in Korea, and shall notify the registry of any change in such agent;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall adopt a code of conduct for all employees and shall provide training on AML and sanctions compliance;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall file all annual reports and financial statements with the registry and the National Tax Service within the statutory deadlines;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall not engage in any activity outside the scope of its business purpose as stated in the Articles of Incorporation, and any such activity shall be void and unenforceable;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall maintain a register of beneficial owners and shall disclose such information to the Financial Intelligence Unit upon request;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall establish a whistleblower policy and shall protect employees who report violations of law or regulation;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall review and update its internal controls annually, and shall engage an external auditor to conduct an annual audit of its financial statements;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall obtain all necessary approvals from the Bank of Korea for any foreign exchange transactions, and shall submit monthly reports on cross-border remittances to the Bank of Korea;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall maintain a contingency plan for business continuity and shall ensure that all customer funds are held in segregated accounts in accordance with applicable regulations;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall not use customer funds for any purpose other than the execution of remittance instructions, and shall return any unclaimed funds to the appropriate authority after the statutory period;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall comply with all sanctions and embargoes imposed by the United Nations, the Republic of Korea, and other relevant jurisdictions, and shall screen all transactions against the consolidated sanctions list;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall appoint a data protection officer and shall register with the Personal Information Protection Commission if required;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall adopt a policy for the retention of records for at least five years, and shall ensure that all records are stored in a secure manner;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall hold an annual general meeting of shareholders within 90 days after the end of each fiscal year, and shall present the financial statements and auditor's report at such meeting;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall not issue any new shares without the approval of the shareholders, and any such issuance shall be made in accordance with the preemptive rights of existing shareholders;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall maintain a register of shareholders and shall update it within 10 days of any transfer of shares;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall adopt a policy for the resolution of disputes, including arbitration, and shall submit to the jurisdiction of the Seoul Central District Court for any legal proceedings;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company shall appoint a statutory auditor if required by law, and shall ensure that the auditor has access to all books and records;

